This repository builds on code and ideas from the following projects. Portions of the code
in fake_quant/ are adapted from them; their copyright notices and licenses continue to apply
to those portions.

* WSVD: Weighted Low-Rank Approximation for Fast and Efficient Execution of Low-Precision
  Vision-Language Models (ICLR 2026) - https://openreview.net/forum?id=zrmQ4koOw9
  LSVD was developed on top of the WSVD code base (Apache License 2.0); the WSVD baseline
  (local fine-tuning / local QAT) is included for comparison.

* QSVD: Efficient Low-rank Approximation for Unified Query-Key-Value Weight Compression in
  Low-Precision Vision-Language Models - https://github.com/SAI-Lab-NYU/QSVD
  (Apache License 2.0). QSVD baseline and gradient-information rank allocation.

* QuaRot: Outlier-Free 4-Bit Inference in Rotated LLMs - https://github.com/spcl/QuaRot
  (Apache License 2.0). Rotation, Hadamard, RTN/GPTQ quantization utilities and the
  fake-quantization framework.

* SVD-LLM: Truncation-aware Singular Value Decomposition for Large Language Model Compression
  - https://github.com/AIoT-MLSys-Lab/SVD-LLM. Cholesky-whitened SVD baseline.

* ASVD: Activation-aware Singular Value Decomposition for Compressing Large Language Models
  - https://github.com/hahnyuan/ASVD4LLM. Activation-aware scaling (--calib_method abs_mean).

* LLaVA - https://github.com/haotian-liu/LLaVA (Apache License 2.0). Model loading for
  LLaVA-v1.5; scripts/setup/convert_sqa_to_llava*.py are adapted from LLaVA
  (see scripts/setup/LICENSE.LLaVA).

* VLMEvalKit - https://github.com/open-compass/VLMEvalKit (Apache License 2.0). Evaluation
  datasets and scoring.

* fast-hadamard-transform - https://github.com/Dao-AILab/fast-hadamard-transform
  (BSD 3-Clause License). Installed as a dependency, not redistributed.

* LightLLM - https://github.com/ModelTC/LightLLM (Apache License 2.0). The flash-decoding Triton
  kernels in kernels/layer_bench/fd_kernel/ are adapted from LightLLM's token-decoding kernels.
